hi my name is Luka from local imperio  comm and today we're going to talk about  love a few weeks ago I was sitting at a  table and attending event and all of a  sudden someone asked me a very peculiar  question we were talking about language  learning and it turned out that I speak  a few languages myself and it had some  foreign partners and this girl asked me  do you pick up girls to learn languages  or do you learn languages to pick up  girls and I had bit that the question  kind of caught me off guard and got me  thinking at the same time so I've been  thinking about my experiences and the  lessons I've learned and here it is I  wanted to share them with you today  the very first important lesson that  I've learned when it comes to speaking  foreign languages with your foreign  partner is that you should at least  speak their language at an intermediate  level I still remember that when I met  my ex French girlfriend I spoke French  relatively well and the same happened  with my ex Russian girlfriend and I am  sure that if I hadn't spoken those  languages at a good level I would have  never spoken or practiced these  languages because we would have reversed  we would have resorted to go figure  English and I've learned that once you  start a relationship in a specific  language that relationship solidifies  and coalesces around the language is  really difficult to change languages  switch languages down the line so the  first lesson I've learned is learn  languages because the more languages you  learn the more opportunities you you  have you never know maybe today you're  going to stumble upon a girl or a guy  who speaks the language you're learning  and remember every language you learn  makes you closer to millions of people  potentially  the second important lesson I've learned  is that language learning doesn't happen  automatically in general and doesn't  happen automatically even if you have a  partner you still have to put in the  effort so you might be thinking that  since you have a partner you might want  to get every chance you get to practice  that language with her or with him but  your partner is your love partner you  share love with them not you know it's  not your he or she is not your language  partner so you have to make a compromise  you have to learn but you don't have to  pester them with too many questions  because otherwise they're going to get -  they're gonna get the idea that you are  there to use them how to do that my  advice is to keep learning on your own  get massive input get into the habit of  listening reading and then also on top  of that you have the chance of  practicing language languages for  example on the internet or with other  friends that's then that's great then  the cherry on the cake is to practice  with your with your partner but that's  the cherry on the cake you should do the  bulk of the work yourself the third  lesson I've learned is that when it  comes to having a foreign partner you  get your fair share of embarrassing  moments of misunderstandings of misusing  words or saying one word thinking that  you're saying something while you're  saying something else meet the parents  meet the circle of friends this is all  part of the beautiful adventure of  having a foreign girlfriend or a foreign  boyfriend so I've had my fair share of  embarrassing moments but I accept them  and I know that this is all part of this  beautiful trip that is a language  learning and getting to know foreign  cultures and foreign people so here you  have it I hope that this was useful if  you have a tandem foreign boyfriend  or girlfriend please share your stories  your everything ranging from  embarrassing situations to  lovely moments with your partner's  families and and friends you can click  in the description box to check on the  link to an article that have written  about this where I share my very  personal stories and in particular my  first kiss in Ireland and how a language  learning played a huge role especially  speaking English with an American accent  made all the difference  [Music]  [Music]
 

